{
  "_comment": [
    "How a Bayer or Flamsteed designation is spelled out, which HYG stores only",
    "as abbreviations: `bayer` as a three-letter Greek stem with an optional",
    "superscript, `con` as the IAU three-letter constellation abbreviation.",
    "",
    "The genitives are the IAU's own, as printed beside the abbreviations in",
    "the list adopted at the 1922 Rome General Assembly and used unchanged by",
    "every star atlas since. Authored here rather than derived: a genitive is a",
    "fact about Latin, not something the coordinates can be asked for.",
    "",
    "tools/catalog.js checks the pair against the 343 names already shipped",
    "before it writes any new ones, so a wrong entry stops generation instead",
    "of quietly renaming a star."
  ],
